Sonic 3 A.I.R. on webOS TVs: "Check for updates" looks for this port's releases

The game's own update check asks Eukaryot's server whether a newer official
build exists for the platform, and "Open download page" opens that page in a
browser. Neither makes sense on a TV: the official downloads do not run
there, the TV has no browser the game can open, and updates for this app come
from this project's GitHub releases (which the Homebrew Channel installs).

With S3W_PORT_UPDATE_CHECK defined (CMakeLists.txt sets it for air_game):
- UpdateCheck asks the port (src/port/PortUpdateCheck.cpp) instead of the
  server: startUpdateCheck() starts its check, performUpdate() polls it, and
  the server's feature list no longer turns the check off.
- The options entry shows the app's version and the latest release's.
- "Open download page" shows the release page's address and a pointer to the
  Homebrew Channel in the port's own menu.
Without the define the game is unchanged.

